{{Illusionnotes
| name = Wild Axes
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus shd}} Non-functional for [[illusions]].
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Wild Axes icon0}}
| desc = Beastmaster sends his axes flying and calls them home again, slicing through enemy units and trees along their path.  Each axe can hit an enemy once, and amplifies subsequent damage from Beastmaster and his units.
}}
* {{Symbol|Projectile|Speed}}
** Has two ability formulas that determines its [[projectile speed]] for both traveling outward and returning:
*** {{cf|expr}}
**** {{Code|ProjectileSpeed {{=}} {{#var:Wild Axes basic1}} , if Distance ≤ {{#var:Wild Axes basic1}}}}
**** {{Code|ProjectileSpeed {{=}} ΣDistance / {{#var:Wild Axes basic2}} , if Distance ≥ {{#var:Wild Axes basic1}}}}
** When returning to Beastmaster, the projectile periodically adapts correspondingly to their distance and the remaining travel time.
** Hence, the axes has a total {{#expr:{{#var:Wild Axes basic2}}*2}}-second max duration while traveling outward and returning.

* {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|beastmaster_wild_axes}}
** The buff is {{M|death dispel|text=death dispellable}} once the {{M|projectiles}} returns to Beastmaster upon his death.

